        "original_id": "a17569bf-8cb0-5df4-ab58-357c28b0f923",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Jesus Jones, The 77s\n- Music releases: Zeroes and Ones, Perverse\n- People: Michael Roe, Mark Harmon, Bruce Spencer\n- Places: Bradford-on-Avon, Wiltshire\n\nFacts:\n- Jesus Jones are a British alternative rock band from Bradford-on-Avon in Wiltshire that formed in late 1988.\n- Jesus Jones recorded and performed from the late 1980s into the 2000s.\n- The 77s are an American rock band whose members include Michael Roe on vocals and guitar, Mark Harmon on bass, and Bruce Spencer on drums.\n- “Zeroes and Ones” is the third single from Jesus Jones’ 1993 album “Perverse.”",
